  "query_preview": "../Sunday through Thursday/...\n\nThe pattern on the synoptic scale moving on into next week remains\nsimilarly active as this weekend. For Sunday and Monday the\nagreement on an upper low being driven into the central Gulf is\nfairly strong, but looking at Tuesday and onward, the eventual\npath of this system is low confidence. As such, expecting a rainy\nand windy situation to close out the weekend and start the\nworkweek. Rain rates will remain consistent, though not as heavy \nas Saturday. The issue will become the persistence of rainfall, as\nprobability of 24 hr ARIs exceeding 2 years is increasing over \n75% for much of the northern panhandle Sunday. \n\nSome convective parameters are indicating support for convection \nwill exist, keeping coastal thunderstorms as a possibility for \nmuch of the time period Sunday and Monday.\n\nBecause the early week system will not be passing its central low\ndirectly through SE AK, winds will settle for the inside channels,\nbut coastal and offshore winds remain stronger over the Gulf. As\nmentioned, there is low confidence in the track for the mid-week \nsystem, but it also appears to be a more poorly formed structure,\nand weather activity reduces late in the week.",
